          "question": "In 1982, residents of Warren County, North Carolina—a predominantly rural, low-income African American community—protested the state's decision to deposit 6,000 truckloads of toxic PCB-contaminated soil in their neighborhood landfill. This historic event launched which national geographic movement?",
