          "stimulus": null,
          "question": "For thousands of years, Australian Aboriginal peoples and Native American nations in California practiced 'cultural burning'—setting low-intensity, controlled mosaic fires across savannas and forests. Why are modern forestry agencies now adopting this traditional practice?",
