            "summary": "Indigenous cultural burning illustrates sophisticated traditional ecological knowledge: frequent, low-heat fires clear accumulated dry forest floor underbrush, stimulate native plant germination, and create natural fuel breaks that stop catastrophic, uncontrollable wildfires.",
